&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Development of modules for the acquisition and visualization of electrical parameters, tracking of voltage, current, active power, reactive power, energy consumed, power factor and frequency, querying of measurement history, graphical data representation and centralized access to information from various monitoring devices.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Functional requirements analysis, design of data models for storing measurements, frontend and backend component development, integration with data acquisition systems, optimization of queries over large volumes of information, functional validation and support for users specialized in energy management.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
ASP.NET MVC, C#, SQL, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Git and technologies focused on enterprise applications for energy monitoring and the supervision of electrical infrastructures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The solution improved the supervision capability of the monitored installations, made it easier to access relevant electrical information, increased the speed of detecting operational incidents and provided a solid foundation for analysis.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; JavaScript, Process automation, ASP.NET MVC, SQL, Web development, Full Stack development, Data modeling, C#&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a id="e007-p001-t005-en"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;E007 - P001 - T005 · Consumption Analysis&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;feb. 2014 - ago. 2014 · 7 months&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Associated with GRUPO J2INGENIEROS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I took part in the design and development of energy consumption analysis features within a monitoring platform used to supervise industrial installations, corporate buildings and service centers. The project was aimed at transforming the data collected by the measurement systems into useful information for identifying consumption patterns and energy improvement opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Facilitate the detailed analysis of electrical consumption through tools that allowed large volumes of information to be interpreted, deviations from expected behavior to be detected and decision-making related to energy efficiency and resource optimization to be supported.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Development of consumption analysis modules, comparative queries between periods, segmentation of information by installation and device, calculation of energy indicators, identification of consumption trends, generation of analytical reports and support tools for energy efficiency studies.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Functional requirements analysis, design of information models, frontend and backend component development, optimization of analytical queries, implementation of energy calculations, functional validation with specialized users and continuous improvement of the platform's analytical capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
ASP.NET MVC, C#, SQL, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Git and technologies focused on enterprise applications for monitoring, data analysis and energy management.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The solution significantly improved the analysis capability of the available energy information, made it easier to detect anomalous consumption, supported energy optimization studies and provided more advanced tools for the efficient management of installations and energy resources.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; Database development, Process automation, ASP.NET MVC, SQL, Web development, Full Stack development, Data modeling, C#&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a id="e007-p001-t004-en"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;E007 - P001 - T004 · Real-Time Visualization&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sept. 2013 - ene. 2014 · 5 months&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Associated with GRUPO J2INGENIEROS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I took part in the design and development of real-time visualization features for an energy monitoring platform focused on the supervision of industrial installations, corporate buildings and service centers. The project focused on providing immediate access to information from electrical measurement systems, making it easier to continuously observe the energy behavior of the monitored installations.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Allow users to view continuously updated information, making it easier to detect incidents early, track energy consumption and operationally supervise installations through accessible, easy-to-interpret graphical tools.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Development of real-time visualization panels, dynamic updating of energy indicators, graphical representation of instantaneous consumption, querying of operational statuses, visualization of alarms and events, tracking of electrical parameters and centralized access to information from multiple measurement devices.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Functional requirements analysis, user interface design, frontend and backend component development, implementation of dynamic data update mechanisms, query optimization and functional validation with users specialized in energy monitoring.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
ASP.NET MVC, C#, SQL, JavaScript, AJAX, HTML, CSS, Git and technologies focused on enterprise applications for real-time supervision and monitoring.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The solution significantly improved the supervision capability of the monitored installations, reduced the time needed to detect operational incidents and provided a more efficient experience for users responsible for the tracking and energy control of complex infrastructures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; JavaScript, Process automation, ASP.NET MVC, SQL, Web development, AJAX, Full Stack development, C#&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a id="e007-p001-t003-en"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;E007 - P001 - T003 · Electrical Circuit Management&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;mar. 2013 - ago. 2013 · 6 months&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Associated with GRUPO J2INGENIEROS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I took part in the design and development of a module for electrical circuit management within an energy monitoring platform intended for industrial installations, corporate buildings and service centers. The project was aimed at structuring and organizing the electrical information of the monitored installations, allowing the various circuits and their relationships with measurement equipment and supervision systems to be represented logically.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Provide a centralized tool for managing electrical circuits, making it easier to organize energy information and allowing a more precise interpretation of the data from the monitoring devices installed across the different infrastructures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Development of modules for creating and managing electrical circuits, association of meters and measurement devices, classification of circuits by type, querying of technical information, management of hierarchical relationships between elements, configuration maintenance and centralized access to the electrical structure of each monitored installation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Functional requirements analysis, data model design, frontend and backend component development, implementation of business rules, optimization of queries related to the electrical structure of the installations, functional validation and collaboration with specialists in energy efficiency and electrical systems.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
ASP.NET MVC, C#, SQL, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Git and technologies focused on enterprise applications for energy monitoring and electrical infrastructure management.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The solution improved the organization of the information associated with the monitored electrical systems, made it easier to manage circuits and measurement devices and increased the traceability of energy data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; JavaScript, ASP.NET MVC, SQL, Web development, Full Stack development, Data modeling, C#&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a id="e007-p001-t002-en"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;E007 - P001 - T002 · Energy Data Capture&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;ago. 2012 - feb. 2013 · 7 months&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Associated with GRUPO J2INGENIEROS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I took part in the design and development of an energy data capture system intended to collect, store and process information from measurement devices installed in industrial infrastructures and buildings. The project was aimed at establishing a solid foundation for energy monitoring, ensuring the availability and reliability of the data later used by the analysis, supervision and reporting modules.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Implement efficient mechanisms for the automatic collection of energy information, allowing the data generated by different measurement devices to be centralized and providing a single source of information for the monitoring platform.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Development of processes for receiving and storing energy readings, validation of received data, management of measurement history, handling of incidents in information capture, normalization of data from different devices, tracking of communication statuses and centralized access to the recorded measurements.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Technical and functional requirements analysis, design of storage structures, development of backend processes for data acquisition and processing, integration with measurement devices, optimization of bulk information loading processes, functional validation and support during rollout phases.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
ASP.NET MVC, C#, SQL, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Git and technologies focused on enterprise applications for the acquisition, storage and processing of energy data.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The solution centralized the information from multiple measurement systems, improved the quality of the energy data available for subsequent analysis, increased the reliability of the capture processes and provided a solid infrastructure for the platform's future evolution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; JavaScript, ASP.NET MVC, SQL, Web development, Software Systems Engineering, Full Stack development, Data modeling, C#&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a id="e007-p001-t001-en"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;E007 - P001 - T001 · Initial Platform Architecture&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;mar. 2012 - jul. 2012 · 5 months&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;em&gt;Associated with GRUPO J2INGENIEROS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
I took part in the design and development of the initial architecture of an energy monitoring platform intended to collect, manage and analyze information from electrical measurement systems. This project was the starting point on which the data capture, circuit management, real-time visualization, consumption analysis, reporting and energy dashboard modules were later built.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Define a solid, scalable and maintainable technological architecture able to support the platform's functional growth, making it easier to integrate new modules and ensuring adequate performance for processing large volumes of energy information.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Features&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Design of the application's general structure, definition of the main data model, implementation of the basic authentication and user management mechanisms, development of the data access architecture, configuration of the communication infrastructure between components and establishment of the foundations for the platform's future evolution.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Functional and technical requirements analysis, software architecture design, database modeling, development of the application's base components, definition of development standards, implementation of common services and validation of the technological structure used as the foundation of the system.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technologies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
ASP.NET MVC, C#, SQL, JavaScript, HTML, CSS, Git and technologies focused on enterprise applications for monitoring, data analysis and energy management.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Result&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The solution provided a robust technological foundation for the platform's growth over the following years, allowing new monitoring, analysis and reporting features to be added without significant redesigns and improving the system's maintainability.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; JavaScript, ASP.NET MVC, SQL, Web development, Backend web development, Software Systems Engineering, Software architecture, Full Stack development, Data modeling, C#&lt;/p&gt;




